In a Wittig reaction, an aldehyde reacts with a halogenoalkane to form an alkene. The conversion is shown in the following unbalanced equation.

{{figure:pdf_visual_04.png}}

Compound $\mathbf{H}$ can be made from propanal, $\text{C}_2\text{H}_5\text{CHO}$. Stage 3 in the reaction scheme is a Wittig reaction.

{{figure:pdf_visual_05.png}}
